34,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Midori,,The joint clinic closed because neither department held the budget. Data agreements take fourteen months.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Readmissions fell a fifth during the trial, but drifted back after. The booking system misses unbooked work.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Nine nursing posts are empty. Agency cover is rising. Midwifery has slack, but therapy staff are leaving.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,The allocation is down a quarter. Off-site visits earn no tariff. On-site sessions bill standard rates.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,Outpatient rooms book out by mid-morning. The shuttle only serves four of nineteen villages.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, the tariff gap is critical. Off-site work is financially invisible to the fund.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, exactly. If it’s not booked, it doesn’t exist. We need visible, billable work.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shion, the staffing gap is real. We can’t rely on agency cover for a new program.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, correct. We need a model that fits the current staffing reality, not an ideal one.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@All, the physical constraints are tight. We must choose a program that fits the existing space.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,The data agreement delay makes outside coordination risky. We need internal control.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"The readmission data suggests home visits work, but only if sustained. The booking gap is a problem.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Misaki,,Midwifery has slack. That’s a resource we can use. Therapy is a drain.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,On-site billing is the only way to recover costs. We need a program that stays on-site.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,The shuttle limitation means we can’t rely on patients traveling far. Local access is key.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,I’m leaning toward a program that doesn’t depend on outside data agreements.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. We need something that shows up in the booking system and the reports.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Misaki,,Using midwifery slack is smart. It avoids the therapy staffing crisis.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"On-site, billable, and staffed by existing slack. That’s the only viable path.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"It must fit the rooms we have. No new construction, just better use of what’s there.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
