60,3,1,talk,Midori,,Candidate D uses midwifery slack. It’s on-site and billable. It avoids the data agreement trap.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"D fits the booking system. It’s visible and reportable. The readmission data supports home visits, but D is safer.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Misaki,,D uses the midwifery team that has slack. It doesn’t burden the therapy or nursing teams.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,"D is on-site, so it bills at the standard rate. It fits the reduced budget.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shizue,,D fits the existing rooms. It doesn’t require new space or shuttle expansion.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, D is the only one that respects the tariff structure. It’s billable and on-site.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, agreed. It’s the only one that shows up in the data. The others are invisible.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shion, D is the only one that doesn’t worsen the staffing crisis. It uses existing slack.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, correct. It’s the only financially sustainable option. The others are liabilities.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@All, D is the only one that fits the physical reality. It’s the practical choice.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Midori,,I vote for D. It’s the most balanced and sustainable choice.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I vote for D. It’s the only one with a clear, measurable impact.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I vote for D. It respects the staffing reality and uses available resources.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,I vote for D. It’s the only one that fits the budget and the tariff structure.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I vote for D. It fits the space and the schedule. It’s the wise choice.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Midori,,"@All, we are in agreement. D is the clear winner.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, confirmed. The data supports it.","{""words"":6,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Jonathan, agreed. The staffing data supports it.","{""words"":7,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, the financial data supports it.","{""words"":6,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, the physical data supports it. Let us proceed.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
